id: pm-rl-local-gate-timing
title: Stabilize local process and card acceptance timings at unchanged bounds
description: "Investigate repeatable local acceptance latency without changing authored limits or coverage scope. In the PR 145 review run, test/process-cli.test.ts reproduced spawnSync ETIMEDOUT alone under its existing command limit, and the canonical 512-case card property in test/policy-card.test.ts reproduced its existing 600000 ms timeout alone. Runs used Node 24, nice, one named test at a time, a fresh home directory and no global/system Git configuration. The same exact fix head 55013729c1e27371e6bd505939b60db151023e19 passed full npm Node 22/26 and Bun Node 26 release gates: 31 policy plus 1489 suite tests per gate, 62 sources, all four coverage dimensions 100 percent. CI evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/41986077627 . The packed LM timing case is already owned by pm-rl-7c7m and is not duplicated here. The HTTP drill and callback matrix passed alone. Preserve every existing test, CLI deadline and coverage threshold while investigating runner/runtime/IO differences. Review refusal fixes remain tracked by pm-rl-proposer-program."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: acceptance,follow-up,timing
